{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1295443-most-mundane-mage","id":1295443,"title":"Most Mundane Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-09T19:32:30-08:00","id":1295443,"title":"Most Mundane Mage","content":"So this is just an interesting concept I had in mind and discussed with my ST, and we have a few ideas about how to build their focus and how they might work in play, but I wondered if anyone on the forums had ideas too. The concept was relatively simple, a character that is ostensibly a mage, but enacts their magick in pretty much the most mundane ways possible. For Life effects they'll go to the doctor and eat healthy food while taking pharmaceuticals to heal, or they go to the gym for a few hours a day to improve their attributes. They'll engage in the use of Prime via the Primal Utility method of &quot;investing&quot; their time and energy into things in order to get superb results, or capitalizing on the efforts and energies of others. Things like that. Certain spheres will certainly be hard to do, but possible I'm sure. I'm just wondering what they should reasonably take for their Focus in terms of belief and practice and instruments, and what group they might best belong to. Thoughts and input are appreciated, it's an interesting idea I hope to play with some day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T05:05:16-07:00","id":1295537,"title":"","content":"It can be more or less anything. Bear in mind that with a few affectations a lot of mages operate more or less like this.<br /> <br /> The thing that I think this is missing is some sense of agency for the character. It's maybe not always clearly stated, but the underlying idea is that your mage is willworking, and your magic in some way needs to represent you implementing your will on reality. Like, Syndicate Hypereconomics doesn't just work by doing accountancy or buying health insurance, it's that by being a superior hypereconomist you have access to special insurance that gives access to cutting-edge medical tech.<br /> <br /> On their own, these are a little too normal. They're not really enacting your mage's will so much as doing the same things as everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:13:58-07:00","id":1295577,"title":"","content":"Reading the title my first thought was the Negation Men, those whose Denial Quiet has made them a sort of magickal sink that counters all nearby will-working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T10:47:21-07:00","id":1295584,"title":"","content":"There used to be a &quot;sleepwalker&quot; flaw for someone who didn't believe they were a mage; as such, at the lowest level of the flaw, they were limited to working only coincidental effects. Not sure if this is what you looking for or thinking of but it is a thing to look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T15:51:14-07:00","id":1295672,"title":"","content":"The Sleepwalker flaw certainly seems like one way to do it, although it does seem somewhat inappropriate in a Mage game, given how expressly the game highlights both new awareness coming with the awakening and how magick is an active force of will. Plus the focus section would be a little weird. <br /> <br /> No, much as I appreciate the idea, I think what I'm looking for is a character that, sure, knows that what they do is &quot;more&quot; than what other people can achieve by the same results, but much like the invigoration etherite or the syndicate op, that's just because he's so much better, his understanding and usage of the seemingly mundane is &quot;enlightened.&quot; Vulgar effects seem hard though. But I can still imagine a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}